+/*
+ * ADC digital volume: the post-ADC gain stage, reg_08 (left) / reg_09 (right).
+ *
+ * The register value maps to gain as
+ *
+ *	gain[dB] = -97 + (reg - 1) * 0.5,	reg = 0x01 .. 0xff
+ *
+ * so 0xc3 is 0 dB, and the reset values picked by _reset_snd_values() are
+ * 0xe1 (+15 dB) on the left channel and 0xf0 (+22.5 dB) on the right one.
+ *
+ * There is no floating point in the kernel, so rather than converting to dB
+ * here - which is what the original vendor code tried to do, and why it ended
+ * up commented out - this is exported in raw register units and the dB mapping
+ * is handed to userspace as a TLV dB scale on the ALSA control.  Keeping the
+ * register value as the control value also means the number amixer reports is
+ * exactly the one "devmem 0x9140e020 32" shows, which helps when a gain
+ * problem has to be debugged against the TRM.
+ */
